desc: Carrier Pigeon Vocoder Carrier (mda VocInput port) by chmaha
tags: vocoder carrier pitch-tracking voice
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Makes a voice-like carrier signal for a vocoder. The input (your voice) passes through unchanged on the
  left channel; the right channel carries a bright sawtooth with breath and sibilance noise, ready to feed the
  carrier input of a vocoder plugin. With Tracking Off the oscillator plays a fixed note; Free follows the
  pitch of the input and Quant snaps it to the nearest semitone, with Pitch as a transpose. Breath adds noise
  to voiced sounds, S Thresh sets how readily consonants get sibilance, and Max Freq is the highest pitch the
  tracker accepts, to keep tracking errors down.
  Ported from mda VocInput by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
